<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osman Sagar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Gandipet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osman Sagar, also called Gandipet, is a reservoir on the Musi river west of Hyderabad, completed in 1920 under the Nizam Osman Ali Khan, after whom it is named. Built after the Musi flood of 1908 killed thousands in the city, it controlled floods and long served as a main source of Hyderabad's drinking water.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osman-sagar.jpg" alt="Osman Sagar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Randhirreddy at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gandipet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
